# Non-secret model/runtime wiring for the ReAct-on-tau2 eval.
#
# Secrets (LITELLM_API_KEY, LITELLM_URL) live in the repo-group .env one level
# up (../.env) and are sourced separately by eval.sh. This file holds only the
# derived, non-secret configuration.
#
# The ReAct agent, the tau2 user simulator, and the NL-assertion judge all route
# through the IBM litellm proxy via litellm's `litellm_proxy/` provider.
# IMPORTANT: for these models we must NOT set OPENAI_BASE_URL / LITELLM_API_BASE
# — doing so makes litellm force custom_llm_provider="openai" and pass the whole
# "litellm_proxy/..." string as an OpenAI model id, which the proxy rejects. The
# litellm_proxy provider reads LITELLM_PROXY_API_BASE / LITELLM_PROXY_API_KEY
# instead (derived in eval.sh from LITELLM_URL + LITELLM_API_KEY).
#
# NOTE: there are no DYNACONF_* behavior-flag settings here — the ReAct agent is
# a native tau2 agent with no extra subsystems to configure.

# --- ReAct agent model ---
# This IS tau2's llm_agent (the ReAct agent is native tau2, not a bridge that
# picks its own model).
# Model casing `Azure/gpt-4.1` (capital A) is enforced by the proxy allowlist.
TAU2_LLM_AGENT=litellm_proxy/Azure/gpt-4.1

# --- tau2 user simulator model ---
TAU2_LLM_USER=litellm_proxy/azure/gpt-5.5

# --- tau2 NL-assertion judge model ---
# tau2's default judge is a bare OpenAI id ("gpt-4.1-2025-04-14") that litellm
# sends to api.openai.com (proxy key rejected). The llm_compat shim reroutes it
# to this proxy model. (gpt-5.5 rejects explicit temperature; the temperature
# shim drops the judge's default temperature=0.0 automatically.)
TAU2_LLM_NL_ASSERTIONS=litellm_proxy/azure/gpt-5.5
